cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below. Status: unpublished research in progress, not peer-reviewed."
title: "TRUST: when do average ratings misrank products compared with uncertainty-aware estimators?"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kefi
    given-names: Mohamed Bechir
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-24"
abstract: "Preregistered simulation study, protocol v1.0 frozen on 2026-11-24; all 1,560 confirmatory runs completed. In this model, shrinkage towards the catalogue mean ranks better than the average rating when ratings are noisy and worse when they are precise; the pooled SHRINK_5 minus MEAN difference in Kendall tau-b is 0.0046 (95% interval 0.0030 to 0.0061), and the advantage reverses under a misspecified shrinkage centre or population shape. All results are simulated; manuscript draft not peer-reviewed. Authorship: Mohamed Bechir Kefi, no affiliation. An AI system was used as a research and development assistant and is not an author. Simulation parameters are calibrated on MovieLens 1M (Harper and Konstan 2015), which is not redistributed."
keywords:
  - rating aggregation
  - Bayesian shrinkage
  - ranking under uncertainty
  - simulation
references:
  - type: article
    title: "The MovieLens Datasets: History and Context"
    authors:
      - family-names: Harper
        given-names: F. Maxwell
      - family-names: Konstan
        given-names: Joseph A.
    journal: "ACM Transactions on Interactive Intelligent Systems"
    volume: 5
    issue: 4
    year: 2015
    doi: 10.1145/2827872
